/-!
# The simply connected root datum of type E7

This file enumerates the 126 roots of type `E7` and builds from them the pinned integral root datum
of type `E₇` on the character and cocharacter lattices `Fin 7 → ℤ`. Coroots are expressed in the
simple-coroot basis and roots in the fundamental-weight basis, so that the `i`-th simple coroot is
the `i`-th standard basis vector and the `i`-th simple root is the `i`-th row of the
Bourbaki-numbered Cartan matrix `CartanMatrix.E₇`. The first seven entries are the Bourbaki simple
roots; the remaining positive roots are ordered by height, followed by their negatives.

Because `E₇` is simply laced, a root and its coroot have the same simple-root coordinates, so a
single stored table determines both: the root coordinates are the Cartan-matrix image of the coroot
coordinates, which is `TauCeti.DynkinType.e7Root_eq_mulVec`. That relation is what makes the root
reflections the image of the coroot reflections under a linear map, so only the coroot half of the
reflection identity needs a table.

Only the coroots are asked to span their lattice, and only that half is recorded, in
`TauCeti.DynkinType.corootSpan_e7SimplyConnectedRootDatum_eq_top`. The roots span the root lattice,
which sits inside the weight lattice with index two, the determinant of `CartanMatrix.E₇`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e7Coroot` and `TauCeti.DynkinType.e7Root`: the coroot and root tables.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e7SimplyConnectedRootDatum`: the pinned root datum of type `E₇`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e7SimpleIndex`: the first seven root indices, the Bourbaki-numbered simple
  roots.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e7SimplyConnectedBase`: the base they form.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.root_e7SimpleIndex` and `TauCeti.DynkinType.coroot_e7SimpleIndex`: the `i`-th
  simple root is the `i`-th row of `CartanMatrix.E₇`, and the `i`-th simple coroot is
  `Pi.single i 1`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.hasCartanType_e7SimplyConnectedRootDatum`: the pinned base has Cartan type
  `E7`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.corootSpan_e7SimplyConnectedRootDatum_eq_top`: the coroots span the
  cocharacter lattice, the simply connected condition.

This is the `E₇` branch of the target "a named datum per valid type" in Layer 6 of
`TauCetiRoadmap/RepresentationTheory/RootSystems/README.md`. It follows Bourbaki, *Lie Groups and
Lie Algebras, Chapters 4--6*, Plate VI.
-/

